    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Apply a Node Patch to the latest synchronized Draft XML and write the result to\r\ntarget_draft.xml. Use --dry-run to validate without writing.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --workspace TEXT:DIR REQUIRED \r\n                              Blueprint workspace directory.\r\n          --patch-file TEXT:FILE REQUIRED \r\n                              Node Patch XML rooted at <patch> with\r\n                              insert/update/delete/replace nodes.\r\n          --dry-run           Validate and summarize the patch without writing\r\n                              target_draft.xml.\r\n          --allow-existing-main-deletion \r\n                              Allow explicit Node Patch deletion or reassignment of existing\r\n                              main segments.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint init  --workspace ./bp_ws --protocol xmldraft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint plan  --workspace ./bp_ws\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint apply --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint cancel\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint commerce --workspace ./bp_ws --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint patch --workspace ./bp_ws --patch-file ./patch.xml\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --ref local://example\r\n\r\nXML TIME LITERALS\r\n  XMLDraft time values are unitless milliseconds.\r\n  Unit suffixes such as us, ms, s, min, or m are rejected.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft blueprint <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
